From 1eb7fef685a09a74bfdfe2943ad29bd71e122557 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:59:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SEO, performance and production hardening

SEO
- Root layout is now a Server Component with full metadata (title template,
  description, canonical, Open Graph, Twitter, robots); client chrome moved
  to layout/AppShell
- Unique title/description/canonical per page via src/lib/seo.ts
- robots.ts, sitemap.ts, generated opengraph-image, styled 404 (real 404)
- JSON-LD: Person, WebSite, ProfilePage, BreadcrumbList, ItemList of projects
- One descriptive H1 per page (decorative "Code"/"Arpit"/loader text demoted)
- CTAs, project cards and Instagram badges are real <a href> links
- Site URL comes from NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL / Vercel (arpitpatidar.com is a
  different person's site); previews are noindexed
- Replaced template copy (Legendarium, lorem subtitles)

Performance
- Removed `unoptimized` from raster images and added `sizes`
  (home page images ~24.6 MB -> ~1.2 MB)
- Stopped preloading a 5.6 MB PNG on the home page
- 9.4 MB audio no longer downloads during page load (preload=none, starts
  after load + idle)
- Hero background: lossless WebP (96 KB -> 38 KB) + high-priority preload
- Intro loader plays once per session
- Image/static caching and security headers in next.config.ts

Correctness / security
- Fixed hydration mismatches in the projects timeline
- Fixed Rules-of-Hooks violation in the lifestyle section
- Contact API: HTML escaping, header-injection guard, length limits,
  honeypot, rate limit, no SMTP error leakage, TLS verification restored
- Labels/aria for form fields and icon-only controls

Adds scripts/seo-check.mjs (npm run seo:check) and .env.example.

